<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Extended results: selective answering</h2>

<figure id="A8.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Selective answering results for all models. Selective answering (Section <a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Hallucination monitoring enables selective answering ‣ 5 Additional experiments ‣ Real-Time Detection of Hallucinated Entitiesin Long-Form Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>) improves conditional accuracy, at the cost of decreasing the total number of questions attempted. The selective answering results displayed here are obtained using a probe threshold of <math id="A8.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t{=}0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t{=}0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A8.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A8.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
