</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.23 110.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:13.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:7.38em;font-size:10pt;" height="110.7" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="192.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A9.F14.pic1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:13.93em;">
<span id="A9.F14.pic1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.F14.pic1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The referee for the rugby match between Georgia and Portugal in the 2022 Rugby Europe Championship on February 6, 2022, was <span id="A9.F14.pic1.p4.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFC8C8;">Christopher Lincoln or ‘Lincoln’</span> <span id="A9.F14.pic1.p4.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#CDEBC8;">but I cannot confirm this, a more reliable source would be needed</span>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span>Example of hallucination detection affecting generation behavior. The baseline Llama-3.3-70B confidently states an incorrect referee name. The LoRA-augmented model exhibits an interesting behavior: it still provides an incorrect answer but immediately acknowledges its uncertainty with “but I cannot confirm this, a more reliable source would be needed.”</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
